  {
    "@id": "https://www.osac.ca/genid/000a1ec2a86e5bec",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Article"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osac.ca/visual-media-arts/event/112-VA4227/invisible-winds-battlefords-allied-arts-council&Itemid=1819"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/inLanguage": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "en-GB"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/articleBody": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n        Invisible Winds\nWed, Aug 19, 2026 to Thu, Oct 1, 2026 @ Chapel Gallery\nCommunity: Battlefords' Allied Arts Council\n\n Education Package\n Condition Report\n List of Works\n Care & Handling\n Press Release\n\n  \n  Jamie, Somatic Winds, Oil on canvas, 30\"x40\"\n\nInvisible Winds:\nStories You Can Not See,\nJourneys toward wholeness\n\nCurated by Dean Bauche, featuring Mary Anne Baxter, Dani Bauche, Dean Bauche, Leah Marie Dorion, Susan Gordon, Iris Hauser, Holly Hildebrand, Roger Jerome, Robert Jerome, Emily Johnson, Karlie King, Bonny Macnab, Jon Philpott, William Philpott, Paul Trottier, Rebecca Toderian, Lyndon Tootoosis, Carol Wylie, and JingLu Zhao.\n\nInvisible Winds is a timely and inspiring exhibition featuring the work of established and emerging artists from across Saskatchewan. It invites us to stop and listen, to see and hear invisible stories carried by so many around us. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nAccompanied by the thoughts of David A. Robertson, author of 'All the Little Monsters' and winner of the Governor General's Literary Award, this exhibition explores issues such as mental health, grief, and the invisibility of trauma in our lives. It highlights the importance of sharing one's story and the necessity of being seen for one's pain to start healing.\n\nInvisible Winds \"honors those with Lived Expertise, [it] uses art to speak that experience to others\".\nRebecca Rackow, Assistant Executive Director\nCanadian Mental Health Association Saskatchewan Division\nOther Exhibitions:\n\nWed, Aug 19, 2026 to Thu, Oct 1, 2026 at Chapel Gallery\nSat, Oct 31, 2026 to Sat, Jan 16, 2027 at St. Thomas More Gallery\nMon, Feb 1, 2027 to Tue, Feb 23, 2027 at Community pARTners Gallery\nMon, Mar 1, 2027 to Tue, Mar 23, 2027 at Brooks Hall\nThu, Apr 1, 2027 to Fri, Apr 23, 2027 at Biggar Museum and Gallery\nSat, May 1, 2027 to Sun, May 23, 2027 at Moosomin Visual Arts Centre\nTue, Jun 1, 2027 to Wed, Jun 23, 2027 at Kindersley Composite School\nThu, Jul 1, 2027 to Sat, Oct 23, 2027 at Grand Coteau Heritage & Cultural Centre\nMon, Nov 1, 2027 to Thu, Dec 23, 2027 at Alex Robertson Public Library- La Ronge\nSat, Jan 1, 2028 to Wed, Feb 23, 2028 at Sherven-Smith Art Gallery\nWed, Mar 1, 2028 to Thu, Mar 23, 2028 at NORVA Centre\nSat, Apr 1, 2028 to Sun, Apr 23, 2028 at Tisdale Community Library\nMon, May 1, 2028 to Fri, Jun 23, 2028 at Station Arts Centre Cooperative\nSat, Jul 1, 2028 to Wed, Aug 23, 2028 at John V. Hicks Gallery at the Margo Fournier Arts Centre\nFri, Sep 1, 2028 to Sat, Sep 23, 2028 at Gallery Works and The Third Dimension\nSun, Oct 1, 2028 to Thu, Nov 23, 2028 at Shurniak Art Gallery\nFri, Dec 1, 2028 to Sat, Dec 23, 2028 at George Layh Theatre\nMon, Jan 1, 2029 to Fri, Feb 23, 2029 at Humboldt and District Gallery\nThu, Mar 1, 2029 to Wed, May 23, 2029 at Art Gallery of Outlook\nFri, Jun 1, 2029 to Sat, Jun 23, 2029 at Gallery on 3rd\n\n    "
      }
    ],
